.TH PHPR 1 "November 2026" "php-rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phpr \- command-line interpreter for PHP scripts (Rust reimplementation)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phpr
.RB [ \-d
.IR key = value ]...
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.IR script.php
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B phpr \-r
.I code
.br
.B phpr \-S
.IR addr : port
.RB [ \-t
.IR docroot ]
.RI [ router.php ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phpr
is the CLI SAPI of the php-rust project, a behaviour-compatible
reimplementation of PHP 8.5.7 written in Rust. It executes unmodified
PHP scripts with the same observable behaviour as the reference
interpreter, byte-for-byte for everything that lands in PHP strings
and output streams. Scripts read from stdin and
.B #!
shebang lines are supported, like the reference CLI.
.PP
On Debian,
.BR update-alternatives (1)
exposes
.B phpr
as
.RI /usr/bin/php
(priority 85), so tools invoking
.B php
keep working. Use
.B "update-alternatives --config php"
to select among installed interpreters (php8.4-cli, php8.6-cli, ...).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " key=value"
Sets the INI entry
.I key
to
.I value
for this process (no
.B =
means an empty value). Only entries the engine implements are
honoured.
.TP
.B \-n
Accepted for compatibility; the reference CLI skips php.ini with it.
.B phpr
never loads a php.ini at all \(em this flag is a no-op.
.TP
.BI \-f " script"
Interpret
.IR script .
.TP
.BI \-r " code"
Run
.I code
inline (implicit leading
.BR "<?php " ).
.TP
.BI \-S " addr:port"
Start the built-in development web server (cli-server SAPI, a
work-alike of
.BR "php \-S" ) .
.TP
.BI \-t " docroot"
Document root for
.BR \-S .
.SH ARGUMENTS
Any argument after the script name is passed to the script via
.B $argv
(as
.B $_SERVER['argv']
). With no script argument the program is read from stdin.
.SH FILES
phpr reads no
.BR php.ini ;
the engine has no configuration file (see
.BR BUGS ).
.SH BUGS
Correct-or-absent is a project rule: what the reference CLI supports
and phpr does not is left out rather than approximated. Currently
absent: the
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-i ,
.B \-l ,
.B \-w
and
.B \-\-ini
switches; loading of php.ini and per-directory INI handling; loading
of binary PHP extensions (the packaged php8.5-* and php8.6-* extension
modules have no effect on
.BR phpr ).
.SH SEE ALSO
For the web server with a worker pool and a systemd service, see
.BR php-server (1).
The reference interpreter:
.BR php (1).
.SH AUTHOR
php-rust by Francesco Tinti. This manual page was written for the
Debian project.
